# Headroom — use it in every chat

Headroom is installed for this Cursor. Setup and limits: `context/HEADROOM.md`.

When the **headroom** MCP server is available, use it. Do not wait for the user to ask.

## Compress

Call `headroom_compress` before reasoning over large tool results, especially:

- Grep / search dumps, test logs, JSON, Excel/markdown ingest
- File reads that are more than a few hundred lines
- Repeated bulky output in the same thread

Keep the compressed text plus the returned `hash`. Do not paste the full original back into the reply.

## Retrieve

If you see a Headroom retrieve marker (`hash=…`) or you need detail that was compressed, call `headroom_retrieve` with that hash. Pass `query` when you only need matching slices.

## Stats

Call `headroom_stats` when the user asks about token savings or whether Headroom is working.

## Do not

- Skip compression on huge tool output “to be safe”
- Treat Headroom as a CrewPulse product feature (it is Cursor tooling; stay inside `context/PRD.md` for app scope)
- Point Cursor-hosted models at the local proxy unless the user is on BYOK and the proxy is running
